## 1. Scope and ownership

These terms apply to Violet Herod's material in this repository. They govern
this repository only; other Briarwood projects carry their own terms.
Source visibility is permission to inspect the work, not an unrestricted
permission to exploit or redistribute its code. Ownership is not transferred.
Third-party material keeps its own notices and licenses. Public facts, abstract
ideas and customer-owned data are not claimed as owned by this notice.

## 2. Free, self-service sample and checker use

You may read the source and download, copy and run the published historical
sample, verification libraries, conformance checks and client tools to prepare
tasks, use the POPCORN service and check its evidence in your own workflows,
including business and agent workflows. Necessary client configuration and
changes to your own task data are allowed. Preserve the copyright, attribution
and permission notices in those copies.

This permission is automatic: ordinary sample, checker and client use requires
no email, negotiated contract, separate written agreement or payment to Violet
Herod. It includes running the demonstrations and testing changed task bytes.
It does not include operating the issuer or a competing witness service.
The resource simulator is available for source inspection; it is not included
in this free client-use grant.

## 3. Paid fresh evidence; receipt use

Fresh signed time or a schedule/task witness is purchased through the hosted
POPCORN service at its published offer, currently $0.001 USDC per request.
Payment is for fresh issuance, not a purchase or license of the issuer software.
Use the normal service payment flow; ordinary customers do not need to negotiate
a separate agreement. No paid request is authorized merely by reading this file.

Recipients may retain, carry, share and verify legitimately issued receipts
without an additional receipt-use royalty, under docs/RECEIPT_USE.md. Those
existing receipt-use terms are unchanged. A receipt does not grant task authority,
prove execution or make a historical observation current.

